From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SheepyLord <37598021+SheepyLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:33:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] The geometry workers sleep when idle instead of polling for
 good

WorkerThreadPool's low-latency mode, which only the geometry workers use (D3D9Rtx::GeometryProcessor,
d3d9_rtx.h:220), let an idle worker poll its queue, try to steal and yield without end: the two
geometry-processing threads each kept a core at 100 % from their first task to the end of the process,
in the main menu too (GMod). An idle low-latency worker now polls as before for kWorkerSpinWindow (1 ms)
after its last task, so the draws within a frame keep their latency, and then sleeps on a condition
variable until a task is counted or the pool stops. Schedule wakes a sleeper only when one sleeps: it
reads an atomic count of sleepers after the push and the task count's increment, and notifies under the
lock; a worker counts itself before it tests for work under that lock, so no wake-up is lost. The
destructor wakes the sleepers. The high-latency mode and the other pools are unchanged.

util_worker_idle.h is self-contained (WorkerSpin, WorkerSleep); tests/rtx/unit/test_worker_idle.cpp
covers the window, a sleeper's wake and stop, a pool shaped like this one (idle workers sleep, a task
wakes them, tasks at the window's edge, workers that cannot steal) and stops with sleeping or polling
workers.
